  "tail": "### FINDING 1 — NONFATAL — location: [L3] in the Facts block\n\n**CLAIM AS WRITTEN:**  \n> and ⊕, ⊗ are monotone in each argument (claims (a), (d), (e) of [[lem-cardinal-arithmetic-basic-laws]]).\n\n**WHY IT FAILS (minor infidelity):**  \nThe actual lemma’s clause (e) states monotonicity only in the **first** argument:\n\n> If κ ≤ λ then κ ⊕ μ ≤ λ ⊕ μ and κ ⊗ μ ≤ λ ⊗ μ; and κ^μ ≤ λ^μ, and μ^κ ≤ μ^λ provided μ ≠ 0.\n\nIt does not explicitly give “in each argument”. The full lemma, via clause (b) commutativity, does imply monotonicity in the second argument, so the mathematical fact is true; the parenthetical citation “(a), (d), (e)” is slightly imprecise because (e) alone does not yield the “each argument” wording.  \n\nThe proof steps that use monotonicity (1.3, 1.4) remain valid — the required inequality κ ⊗ 1 ≤ κ ⊗ λ (from 1 ≤ λ) follows from commutativity and the first‑argument monotonicity actually stated in (e). This is a minor citational quirk, not a mathematical error.\n\n---\n\n### Step‑by‑step verification\n\n- **Step 1.1** – Correct. The injection ξ ↦ (0,ξ) from κ into κ ⊔ λ gives κ ⪯ κ ⊔ λ. By [L3] (well‑orderable sets) and [L4] (|κ| = κ) together with [L2] (definition of ⊕) we obtain κ ≤ κ ⊕ λ.\n- **Step 1.2** – Correct. The map (i,ξ) ↦ (ξ,i) is defined on κ ⊔ κ = ({0}×κ) ∪ ({1}×κ); for any element ξ ∈ κ and i ∈ {0,1} ⊆ κ (by [L5]), so the image lies in κ × κ. The map is plainly injective. The judge’s concern about “λ‑tagged elements” appears to be a misreading — the step involves only κ ⊔ κ, not κ ⊔ λ.\n- **Step 1.3** – Correct. λ ≤ κ together with monotonicity of ⊕ and ⊗ (available from the cited lemma, either directly or via commutativity) yields κ ⊕ λ ≤ κ ⊕ κ and κ ⊗ λ ≤ κ ⊗ κ.\n- **Step 1.4** – Correct. λ ≠ 0 implies 0 ∈ λ (ordinal basics, [L6]), whence {0} = 1 ⊆ λ, so 1 ≤ λ. The unit law κ ⊗ 1 = κ is part of [L3] (clause (d)), and monotonicity gives κ ⊗ 1 ≤ κ ⊗ λ, so κ ≤ κ ⊗ λ.\n- **Step 2.1** – Correct. Step 1.2 provides an injection κ ⊔ κ → κ × κ. By [L3] (well‑orderable sets) we get |κ ⊔ κ| ≤ |κ × κ|, which by [L2] is κ ⊕ κ ≤ κ ⊗ κ. Hessenberg [L1] gives κ ⊗ κ = κ, so κ ⊕ κ ≤ κ.\n- **Step 3.1** – Correct. Chaining the inequalities and using antisymmetry of ordinal inclusion ([L6]) gives κ ⊕ λ = κ and, for λ ≠ 0, κ ⊗ λ = κ. The λ = 0 case is handled by the unit law κ ⊗ 0 = 0 from [L3].\n\n**Overall:** The proof is mathematically sound, every step is licensed by the facts it cites (the one minor imprecision in the Facts block does not affect any deduction), and the title accurately reflects what is proved.\n\n**Checked:** the Statement, the entire Facts block against every dependency text, all proof steps 1.1–3.1, the Remarks for false claims about other items (none found that affect the item), and the specific points about unit law, monotonicity, and the λ = 0 exception — all are handled correctly.\n\n0 fatal, 1 nonfatal"
